# Clerk's publishable key (S21). Safe to expose: it identifies the Clerk application to the
# browser and grants nothing on its own. The SECRET key is the backend's and belongs in the
# backend's own environment — it must never appear in this file or in any built asset.
#
# Leave it unset and the app still builds and runs, with Clerk's sign-in simply not present.
# That is the mode vitest, CI and the Playwright journeys run in, and the mode a contributor
# with no Clerk account gets. It is not a degraded build; it is the keyless one.
#
# To fill it in: create an application at https://clerk.com (or run `npx clerk init` from this
# directory, which creates one against your own Clerk account) and copy the publishable key.
# See docs/RUNBOOK.md for the rest of the provisioning, including the three free social
# connections and the backend's GURU_CLERK_* settings.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Where the API answers. Defaults to http://localhost:8000, matching the backend's dev CORS.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
